<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugoslav MiG-21 crashes near Belgrade.</title>
<headline>Yugoslav MiG-21 crashes near Belgrade.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Yugoslav airforce MiG-21 fighter plane crashed near the Batajnica military airfield near Belgrade on Wednesday, the state-run news agency Tanjug reported.</p>
<p>According to the report, the aircraft crashed at 10:59 a.m. when a bird flew into the engine and caused a &quot;flameout&quot;.</p>
<p>Quoting from an airforce statement, Tanjug said the pilot ejected safely and the plane crashed. There were no casualties.</p>
</text>
